// KNOWN GAP (`&&T` in code generation, PLAN.md Phase 5 "`Ref<T>`"): auto-deref through two
// references to a tuple. rustc prints 3; Sabiko type-checks and borrow-checks it but code
// generation rejects the `&&(..)` local (E0500, "a reference to a reference"). Split out of
// `differential/run/tuples/refs.sabi`; belongs back there once `&&T` lowers.
fn Main() {
    let t = (1, (2, 3));
    let r = &t;
    let rr = &r;
    PrintLine(rr.1.1);
}
